{"id":"chapter-004","n":4,"title":{"en":[["Chapter","","t"]," ",["Three","","a"],":"," ",["The","","a"]," ",["Physical","","t"]," ",["Characteristics","","t"]," ",["of","","f"]," ",["Kappas","","d"]],"zh":[["第","dì","t"],["三","sān","t"],["章","zhāng","t"],"：",["河","hé","t"],["童","tóng","t"],["的","de","f"],["身","shēn","t"],["体","tǐ","t"],["特","tè","t"],["征","zhēng","t"]],"ja":[["三","さん","t"]]},"p":[{"id":"kappa-akutagawa-s004-p00011","src":"Before I continue my story, I must pause to explain a little about what kappas are. The kappa is an animal whose very existence is still a matter of doubt. Yet since I myself lived among them, there can surely be no room for doubt. As for what kind of animal it is, it has short hair on its head and webbed hands and feet, just as described in works such as A Brief Study of the Water Tiger, with no striking differences. They stand roughly a meter tall, perhaps a little over or a little under. According to the doctor, Chack, they weigh between twenty and thirty pounds, though he said that on rare occasions there are great kappas weighing fifty-odd pounds. In the middle of the head is an oval dish, which apparently grows progressively harder with age. Indeed, the dish of the elderly Bag feels entirely different from that of the young Chack. But the strangest thing of all is surely the color of a kappa's skin. Unlike us human beings, kappas have no fixed skin color. Somehow they change to match the color of their surroundings—for example, among grass they turn green like grass, while on a rock they turn gray like the rock. This ability, of course, is not peculiar to kappas; chameleons possess it as well. Perhaps the structure of a kappa's skin is in some respect similar to that of a chameleon. When I discovered this fact, I recalled a folkloric record stating that the kappas of western Japan are green, while those of the northeast are red. I also remembered how, when I was chasing Bag, he had suddenly vanished from sight, leaving me unable to tell where he had gone.","u":[{"en":[["Before","","f"]," ",["I","","s"]," ",["continue","","p"]," ",["my","","a"]," ",["story","","o"],","," ",["I","","s"]," ",["must","","p"]," ",["pause","","p"]," ",["to","","f"]," ",["explain","","p"]," ",["a","","a"]," ",["little","","a"]," ",["about","","f"]," ",["what","","o"]," ",["kappas","","s"]," ",["are","","p"],"."," "],"zh":[["在","zài","f"],["继","jì","p"],["续","xù","p"],["讲","jiǎng","p"],["下","xià","p"],["去","qù","p"],["之","zhī","o"],["前","qián","o"],"，",["我","wǒ","s"],["得","dé","f"],["先","xiān","d"],["稍","shāo","d"],["微","wēi","d"],["说","shuō","p"],["明","míng","p"],["一","yī","o"],["下","xià","o"],["河","hé","o"],["童","tóng","o"],["究","jiū","d"],["竟","jìng","d"],["是","shì","p"],["什","shén","a"],["么","me","a"],["样","yàng","a"],["的","de","f"],["动","dòng","o"],["物","wù","o"],"。"],"ja":[["僕","ぼく","s"],["は","","f"],["この","","a"],["先","さき","o"],["を","","f"],["話","はな","p"],["す","","p"],["前","まえ","d"],["に","","f"],["ちょっと","","d"],["河童","かっぱ","d"],["と","","f"],["いう","","p"],["もの","","o"],["を","","f"],["説明","せつめい","p"],["し","","p"],["て","","f"],["おか","","p"],["なけれ","","p"],["ば","","f"],["なり","","p"],["ませ","","p"],["ん","","p"],"。"],"src":"Before I continue my story, I must pause to explain a little about what kappas are. "},{"en":[["The","","a"]," ",["kappa","","s"]," ",["is","","p"]," ",["an","","a"]," ",["animal","","a"]," ",["whose","","f"]," ",["very","","d"]," ",["existence","","s"]," ",["is","","p"]," ",["still","","d"]," ",["a","","a"]," ",["matter","","o"]," ",["of","","f"]," ",["doubt","","d"],"."," "],"zh":[["河","hé","s"],["童","tóng","s"],["是","shì","p"],["一","yī","o"],["种","zhǒng","o"],["至","zhì","d"],["今","jīn","d"],["仍","réng","a"],["令","lìng","p"],["人","rén","d"],["怀","huái","p"],["疑","yí","p"],["是","shì","p"],["否","fǒu","p"],["真","zhēn","d"],["实","shí","d"],["存","cún","p"],["在","zài","f"],["的","de","f"],["动","dòng","o"],["物","wù","o"],"。"],"ja":[["河童","かっぱ","s"],["は","","f"],["いまだ","","d"],["に","","f"],["実在","じ